## Proposed Changes

### 1. Comprehensive System Documentation (`docs/`)

Per `Starter.md` (Sections 1-8, 11-12, 38, 48, 60), establish authoritative documentation to govern all development.

#### [NEW] [ARCHITECTURE.md](file:///d:/Codingh/Task%20Managemnt%20System/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Complete System Map:
  - Frontend (Next.js App Router, React Server/Client Components, Tailwind CSS, Lucide icons)
  - API / Controller Layer (`app/api/*` route handlers with centralized validation and auth wrappers)
  - Service Layer (`lib/services/*` business logic, transaction boundaries, state machines)
  - Data Access / Repository Layer (`lib/repositories/*` or typed Prisma client queries)
  - Database (PostgreSQL with strict constraints and indexes)
- State management, concurrency defense (optimistic locking, atomic operations), error handling architecture, and observability strategy.

#### [NEW] [DATABASE_SPEC.md](file:///d:/Codingh/Task%20Managemnt%20System/docs/DATABASE_SPEC.md)
- Formal Relational Schema for PostgreSQL:
  - `users` (id, name, email, passwordHash, role, createdAt, updatedAt)
  - `tasks` (id, title, description, status, priority, dueDate, createdById, assignedToId, version, createdAt, updatedAt)
  - `comments` (id, taskId, authorId, content, createdAt, updatedAt)
  - `activities` (id, taskId, userId, action, metadata, createdAt)
- **Normalization Verification**: Explicit 1NF, 2NF, 3NF, and BCNF analysis per `Starter.md` Section 5.
- **Database Invariants**: Foreign key relationships, `ON DELETE CASCADE` / `SET NULL` policies, check constraints (e.g. enum validation, valid status transitions), and index definitions (`tasks(status, priority)`, `tasks(assignedToId)`, `comments(taskId, createdAt)`).

#### [NEW] [SECURITY_RBAC.md](file:///d:/Codingh/Task%20Managemnt%20System/docs/SECURITY_RBAC.md)
- **Access Control Matrix**:
  - Roles: `ADMIN`, `MANAGER`, `MEMBER`
  - Granular permissions: Task creation, assignment, status transition, editing, deletion, user management, and comment authorship.
- **Threat Model & OWASP Mitigation Matrix**:
  - Server-side identity & authorization enforcement (preventing IDOR/BOLA).
  - Input sanitization (XSS defense).
  - Parameterized ORM queries (SQLi defense).
  - CSRF/SameSite cookie strategies and secure HTTP headers.
  - Rate limiting parameters for auth & mutation endpoints.

#### [NEW] [API_CONTRACTS.md](file:///d:/Codingh/Task%20Managemnt%20System/docs/API_CONTRACTS.md)
- REST API contracts for all endpoints:
  - Auth: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me`
  - Tasks: `GET /api/tasks`, `POST /api/tasks`, `GET /api/tasks/:id`, `PATCH /api/tasks/:id`, `DELETE /api/tasks/:id`
  - Status & Workflow: `PATCH /api/tasks/:id/status` (state-machine transition)
  - Comments: `GET /api/tasks/:id/comments`, `POST /api/tasks/:id/comments`, `DELETE /api/comments/:id`
  - Users: `GET /api/users` (for task assignment, scoped by role)
  - Activity: `GET /api/tasks/:id/activities`
- Explicit Request DTOs, Response schemas, and RFC 7807 compliant error format.

